<h2>Project Description</h2>
<p>
  PermitGPT is an AI-powered permitting assistant designed to simplify the construction
  permit process for homeowners, contractors, developers, and municipalities.
</p>

<h2>Problem Statement</h2>
<p>
  Construction permitting is slow, confusing, and inconsistent across cities and counties.
  Homeowners, contractors, and small developers often struggle to identify required
  documents, understand local rules, and predict approval risks.
</p>

<h2>Project Scope</h2>
<ul>
  <li>AI-driven permit guidance</li>
  <li>Permit readiness scoring</li>
  <li>Smart document checklist generation</li>
  <li>Approval-risk prediction</li>
  <li>Jurisdiction-based permit recommendations</li>
  <li>User-friendly dashboard interface</li>
  <li>Future integration with municipal permitting systems and APIs</li>
</ul>

<h2>Target Market</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Homeowners</li>
  <li>Small contractors</li>
  <li>Real estate developers</li>
  <li>Construction companies</li>
  <li>Architects and engineers</li>
  <li>Municipal permitting departments</li>
  <li>Permit expeditors</li>
  <li>Smart city and GovTech organizations</li>
</ul>

<h2>Prototype / Proof of Concept</h2>
<p>
  The early prototype will demonstrate how PermitGPT can guide users through permit
  readiness by asking simple questions, identifying missing documents, and providing
  a readiness score before submission.
</p>

